// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`ServiceGatewayTool description enumerates every capability in CAPABILITY_MAP (snapshot) 1`] = `
"service-gateway: invoke an approved READ-ONLY tenant-scoped backend capability.
Returns a structured envelope that the frontend renders as tables, charts, or metrics.

MANDATORY ROUTING (you MUST follow these exactly):
  • User says "dashboard" or "summary" or "metrics" or "stats" or "overview" → MUST use: getDashboardSummary
  • User says "customers" or "customer list" or "all customers" or "my customers" → MUST use: listCustomers
  • User says "projects" or "project list" or "all projects" or "my projects" → MUST use: listProjects

Capability list:
  - listProjects: List projects in the tenant with optional filters
  - getProject: Read a single project by ID
  - listCustomers: List customers in the tenant
  - getCustomer: Read a single customer by ID
  - listGoals: List goals in the tenant with optional filters
  - getGoal: Read a single goal by ID
  - listTasks: List tasks in the tenant with optional filters
  - getTask: Read a single task by ID with execution logs
  - listDepartments: List departments in the tenant
  - getDepartment: Read a single department by ID
  - listAgents: List AI agents in the tenant with optional filters
  - getAgent: Read a single agent by ID with capabilities
  - listApprovals: List approval requests in the tenant
  - getApproval: Read a single approval request by ID
  - getDashboardSummary: Aggregate dashboard summary (agents, tasks, departments, approvals, costs)
  - listWorkflows: List workflows in the tenant with optional filters
  - getWorkflow: Read a single workflow by ID
  - listDeliverables: List deliverables in the tenant
  - getDeliverable: Read a single deliverable by ID
  - listAssignments: List eligible agents for assignment
  - listInboxItems: List inbox items for a user within the tenant
  - getInboxItem: Read a single inbox item by ID
  - getCostReport: Aggregate tenant cost summary over a date window
  - getCostByDepartment: Cost breakdown for a department over a date window
  - getCostByAgent: Cost breakdown for an agent over a date window
  - getComplianceStatus: Read compliance checklist status for the tenant
  - knowledgeSearch: Search the tenant knowledge base by free-text query
  - listConnectors: List CRM connectors configured for the tenant
  - getConnectorStatus: Read a single CRM connector by ID
  - listIntegrationCredentials: List third-party integrations (Google, Brevo, …) for the tenant
  - getIntegrationStatus: Aggregate connection status for Google + Brevo integrations
  - listWorkRuns: List recent governed work runs for the tenant (best-effort; falls back to empty when the underlying repo exposes no list method)
  - getWorkRun: Read a single work run by ID with current state
  - commandCenterSummary: Aggregate platform command-center summary (timeline, alerts, kpis)

IMPORTANT: When user asks for "dashboard" or "summary" or "metrics" → use getDashboardSummary (NOT listProjects).
IMPORTANT: When user asks for "customers" → use listCustomers (NOT getDashboardSummary).
IMPORTANT: When user asks for "projects" → use listProjects.
IMPORTANT: Never perform a mutation through this tool. Mutations use the governed HITL tool path.

If user asks for something that does not match any capability above, respond with a plain text apology.

Format: { capability: "<name>", params: { ... } }."
`;
